linked = sum(bool(links[i]['rob2_assessment_id']) for i in members)
new_candidates = {i for i in members if not links[i]['rob2_assessment_id'] and candidate_by[i]}
doc(R/'ROB2_PROVENANCE_RECONCILIATION_v37.md', f'''# RoB 2 provenance reconciliation — v37

{STAMP}

Non-sensitivity bodies: {len(grade)}; unique component results: {len(members)}; currently linked: {linked}; unlinked: {len(members)-linked}. Existing candidates found for {len(new_candidates)} of the unlinked results; {len(members)-linked-len(new_candidates)} lack such a candidate. These counts describe applicability work, not approval. Current canonical linkage remains 97/761. No GRADE certainty category or RoB vector was changed.

`02_DECISIONS/v37/rob2_non_sensitivity_worklist.csv` has one row per component result, including separate active arms before combination. `rob2_existing_candidates.csv` preserves historical assessment vectors, source row/version identities, recorded adopters/dates and rationale. Historical v34 source registers contain textual claims of review-lead adoption; these are evidence of recorded adoption, not independently verified dual review. The linker's hard-coded date placeholders cannot establish absence of upstream adoption.

## Version conflicts requiring decisions

- Luo nausea48: selected AF26-D-008 is High (D4 High); corrected record CORRECTED-V34-031 is Some concerns; historical priority-2 record is Low and assumes effective masking. Source allocation guesses were 77.5% and 66.2% (`ASTRA_VERIFICATION_SUPPORT/source_text/covidence_35_verified.txt:370`). Do not transfer the historical approval to the selected High vector or automatically revise GRADE. Nausea rationale now references 77 nausea events, not vomiting events; inherited Low certainty remains pending review.
- Xiong PONV48: source has no-current electrodes (`ASTRA_VERIFICATION_SUPPORT/source_text/covidence_431_full_article.txt:142`); sham classification stays. Current corrected RoB record says antiemetics alone; reconcile D2/comparator wording and the alternative AF26-D-003 High assessment.
- El-Rakshy: `07_risk_of_bias/RoB2_ElRakshy_2009_MorphineConsumption_24h.md` records Mendoza adoption 9 Sep, but D2 Some concerns differs from selected D2 Low. The dated adoption cannot be copied to that selected vector.
- Ng flatus V33-OD-0117: historical priority-2 adoption 8 Sep matches the selected domain vector. Retain as provenance, not independent final sign-off.
- Pan vomiting AUDIT-0100: historical candidate says 105 randomized/analyzed; source describes 120 enrolled and subsequent exclusions. Revisit D3 before accepting it.
- Zheng flatus AUDIT-0347: source endpoint definition refers to first stools (`01_SOURCE_EVIDENCE/Zheng_2025.txt:200`); clarify gas versus defecation as well as SD/P inconsistency. Source values and model membership remain unchanged; leave-out diagnostic retained.

## Linker limitations — explicitly not certified

The inherited register contains {len(reg)} rows and {len(counts)} distinct assessment IDs; {sum(n>1 for n in counts.values())} IDs are reused. `rob2_id_collisions.csv` gives row-specific identities. Automatic AF selection tests study, comparison ID and statistics but lacks an explicit semantic outcome/window gate; equal counts alone are not sufficient. These limitations require version-specific reconciliation before final lock. Candidate records are deliberately not imported into canonical selections as if approved.

Do not extend assessments across Zhu active arms, Lu PC6/combined-site arms, Sun timing arms, Huang ipsilateral/contralateral arms, Ng sham/no-acupuncture controls, or Oztas usual-care/active-TENS controls. Szmit's usual-care primary opioid result remains unassessed. The current vomiting24 TEAS/sham model has 4 trial contrasts, not the obsolete 5.
''')

